% SCAFFOLDING stand-in for SIMPOS's class `network_node_name` (this PSI's
% name on the network), compiled by psi/espc.py into the package
% `simpos`.  It is NOT SIMPOS: no part of it is printed or held.  Every
% method is INTERPOLATED (labelled), from:
%   - docs/simpos/subsystems/shell.md §2.3 and notes/fixpoint.tsv row
%     `network_node_name get_my_node 2` (USAGE): PIMOS's
%     src_util/pmeter/xrmonitor.esp:27-31 (held IFS source, 1992),
%     `:get_my_node(#network_node_name, ^Node)` gives this PSI's node name
%     string, used as a host name (the attribute default there is a host
%     name of the form `fkpsi602`);
%   - pimfep##fep_node_table (held .ptf, cells read 2026-11-24): its
%     initiate/1 stores `:get_my_node(#network_node_name, N)` with
%     set_local_node_name/2, and its local_node_name/2, when that slot is
%     still `none`, stores `:node_name(#network_node_name, N)` the same
%     way.  So both name the local node (INFERENCE from the two
%     call sites; no source says they differ).
% Model (OURS): one class slot holding the name; the string "psi" is OURS
% (the real default is not known; shell.md's `fkpsi602` is one site's).
% node_full_name/3 and node_type/3 (also sent by held code) are not
% stood in.

class network_node_name has

% INTERPOLATED: the representation and the value (OURS; see above).
attribute my_node := "psi";

% INTERPOLATED from: xrmonitor.esp:27-31; fep_node_table initiate/1.
:get_my_node(Class, Node) :- Node = Class!my_node;

% INTERPOLATED from: fep_node_table local_node_name/2 (see above).
:node_name(Class, Node) :- Node = Class!my_node;

end.
